# Pipeline validation

- Run `python scripts/validate-workflow-guardrails.py` after pipeline changes.
- Run manifest and schedule schema validation after config/schema changes.
- Run `actionlint` after workflow changes and `shellcheck` after shell changes.
- Validation must fail on errors; do not downgrade lint failures to warnings.
- Every workflow must declare explicit top-level `permissions`.
- Prefer the minimum permission set and elevate only in the job that needs it.
- New scheduled manifest names must resolve to an existing manifest file.
- New external checkouts must use a separate `path`.
- Tests for guardrails must include both a passing and a failing fixture or
  exercise the failure condition against a temporary copy.
- Keep CI checks deterministic: use pinned tool/action versions and avoid
  downloading an unversioned `latest` release.
- A guardrail regex that extracts one field's value from a multi-line YAML
  `with:` block (e.g. `manifest_name`) must not also match sibling fields on
  later lines (e.g. `target_environment`, `tag_name`) that happen to look like
  the first field's expression. Scope the capture to that field's own
  line/expression; do not key the end-boundary on "next key" when the matched
  span can itself contain other key-like or value-like text. (Root cause of a
  real CI failure: the frontend schedule's `target_environment`/`tag_name`
  values were misread as manifest names.)
- Guardrail tests must be parameterized (loop + `subTest`), not a single
  hardcoded fixture. When fixing a guardrail bug, add the exact values that
  caused the false positive/negative as one case, plus at least one additional
  case with different values, so the fix is proven general and not just
  memorized for one literal string.
- Before claiming "CI passes" or "ready to ship," run every check CI runs that
  is runnable locally (Python test suites, `validate-workflow-guardrails.py`,
  `check-jsonschema` per manifest/schedule file, `bash -n` on every changed
  script) and explicitly name any step you could not run locally (missing
  `jq`/`shellcheck`/`actionlint` binary) instead of assuming it would pass.
